    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate the mean number of times students in this random sample go online.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2.6$ times",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sum fx&=0(8)+1(3)+2(5)+3(6)+4(7)+5(5)+6(0)+7(1)\\\\\\sum fx&=91\\\\\\overline{x}&=\\frac{91}{35}\\\\\\overline{x}&=2.6\\end{align*}$$\nThe mean is $2.6$ times.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the standard deviation of the number of times students go online, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.90$ times",
          "worked": "Using the frequency-weighted squared deviations:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum f(x-2.6)^2&=8(6.76)+3(2.56)+5(0.36)+6(0.16)\\\\&\\quad+7(1.96)+5(5.76)+0(11.56)+1(19.36)\\\\\\sum f(x-2.6)^2&=126.4\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{126.4}{35}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx1.90\\end{align*}$$\nThe standard deviation is $1.90$ times, correct to two decimal places.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the range of times online that lie within one standard deviation of the mean.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$ to $4$ times, inclusive.",
          "worked": "Using the unrounded standard deviation:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}-\\sigma&=2.6-\\sqrt{\\frac{126.4}{35}}\\approx0.70\\\\\\overline{x}+\\sigma&=2.6+\\sqrt{\\frac{126.4}{35}}\\approx4.50\\end{align*}$$\nThe whole-number counts in this interval are $1,2,3,4$. Thus the range is $1$ to $4$ times, inclusive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If every student in this sample went online one more time than what was recorded, determine the effect on the mean and standard deviation.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The mean increases by $1$, from $2.6$ to $3.6$ times. The standard deviation remains $1.90$ times.",
          "worked": "Adding $1$ to every value also adds $1$ to the mean, so the new mean is $2.6+1=3.6$ times.\n\nEach deviation is unchanged because $(x+1)-(\\overline{x}+1)=x-\\overline{x}$. Therefore the standard deviation remains $\\sqrt{\\frac{126.4}{35}}\\approx1.90$ times.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
